  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Development Programme, Afghanistan Country Office - Afghanistan (01-Oct-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Afghanistan, Malaria, United Nations Development Programme (UNDP Afghanistan)This program has the following goals: To contribute to the improvement of the health status in Afghanistan through the reduction of morbidity and mortality associated with malaria. The objectives of this program are: To reduce malaria morbidity by 85% in all malaria stratum by the end of 2017.  To reduce malaria morbidity in high risk areas (stratum one districts) by 80% by the end of 2017.  To reduce malaria mortality to zero by the end of 2017.  To reduce the incidence of P. falciparum malaria to sporadic cases by the end of 2017 with a vision to completely interrupt transmission of Pf by 2020</narrative>
  </description>
